C[The white stone at F8 has two liberties: one towards the edge, one towards the centre. Give atari from the right side and it has nowhere to run.

Task: Capture the white stone, however it runs.]
(;B[fc]C[RIGHT F7 gives atari from the centre side, so White can only run towards the edge, where it runs out of liberties.])
(;B[ec]C[RIGHT E7 does not even touch the stone, but it closes the way out: wherever White runs, you can capture it against the edge. This is called a net.])
(;B[gc]C[RIGHT G7 does not even touch the stone, but it closes the way out: wherever White runs, you can capture it against the edge. This is called a net.])
(;B[fd]C[RIGHT F6 does not even touch the stone, but it closes the way out: wherever White runs, you can capture it against the edge. This is called a net.])
